Async Python Project
Overview
This project focuses on asynchronous programming in Python using the asyncio module. It demonstrates how to use the async and await syntax to run tasks concurrently and efficiently manage asynchronous I/O operations.

Learning Objectives
By completing this project, you will gain a strong understanding of:

How to work with async and await syntax to define asynchronous functions.
How to execute an async program using the asyncio library.
Running concurrent coroutines to handle multiple tasks at the same time.
Creating and managing tasks in asyncio to control the flow of asynchronous programs.
Using the random module to introduce randomness in the execution of tasks.
Requirements
All code is written and tested using Python 3.7 on Ubuntu 18.04 LTS.
Files follow the pycodestyle style guide (version 2.5.x) and include type annotations.
Each module and function is well-documented, explaining its purpose and usage.
The project includes asynchronous functions that are run concurrently using asyncio.
Resources
To fully grasp the concepts presented in this project, refer to:

Async IO in Python: A Complete Walkthrough
asyncio - Asynchronous I/O (Python official documentation)
random.uniform function from the random module.
